# GitHub issue fixes

When implementing a fix for a numbered GitHub issue (e.g. from the tech-debt backlog):

- **Do not** run `gh issue close` or mark the issue complete in comments unless the user explicitly asks you to close it.
- **Do** implement the fix, run tests, and briefly tell the user which issue was addressed and how to verify.
- The user closes the issue after they test on their machine or the NUC.

When the user asks to close a **parent issue** that has sub-issues (e.g. [#30](https://github.com/rfreedman/dvra-repeater-announcements/issues/30), [#31](https://github.com/rfreedman/dvra-repeater-announcements/issues/31)), close **all linked sub-issues in the same turn**, then the parent, unless they say otherwise.

Optional: add a finding row to `docs/code-review-findings.md` when the fix matches a documented review item.
